{
  "name": "Riso Ink Colours",
  "description": "Risograph duplicator ink drums as sRGB approximations. Each entry is one ink drum: a Riso print is built by overprinting one drum per pass, so these are SPOT colours, not process colours - `book` names the ink book a separation would carry (see SpotColor in packages/core/src/host-v1.ts). The hex is an approximation of the ink on white uncoated stock: Riso ink is translucent and soy-based, so real output shifts with paper, coverage and drum age. Ordered as Riso lists them: standard drums first, then the extended/custom range.",
